  middlegame. DO NOT retry; eval path = Folkert retrain pipeline only.

2026-08-17 desktop clock investigation (board NPS R&D):
- Found 5 orphaned Dog engine processes (Aug 15-16) eating ~400% CPU
  (Dog-base-qsee 2847 CPU-min, Dog-native, Dog-ruk x2, Dog-256-base);
  killed. They polluted every load>1 measurement since Aug 15.
- After cleanup: bench2 microbench (make+eval+unmake loops) still measured
  69-2500 us/op while the real search does 190k nodes in 0.38s wall.
- Root cause: esp_timer_get_time() on the DESKTOP (gettimeofday vDSO) is
  unreliable on this board: deltas inflated ~2x-1000x (varies with
  interval). Verified: inline cntvct_el0 (134 ticks @54MHz = 2.48us) and
  inline CLOCK_MONOTONIC (2.53us) agree with each other AND with wall
  clock (time); the function-call path through the shim reports 1000x.
  Rebuilding with clock_gettime/cntvct shims did NOT fix it (still lies);
  direct inline reads are truthful. Reverted shim to gettimeofday.
- Consequences: desktop absolute nps claims are garbage (real ~540k nps
  on depth-12, not 269k); RELATIVE same-session comparisons remain valid
  (both engines under same distortion) - ruk512/ruk256 rejections stand.
  Board (ESP32) uses hardware esp_timer - its 7100 nps was always real.
  Desktop matches: cutechess enforces wall clock, engines never exceed
  budget - match verdicts unaffected.
- Real desktop eval-machinery costs (inline cntvct/mono): pos make+unmake
  ~1.5us, eval-makeonly ~6us, nnue_evaluate ~1us, full op ~15us. Scalar
  but normal - nothing pathological. PIE SIMD for add_feature/remove_
  feature (256-int16 loops, ~3.5 instr/elem) remains the board candidate.
- New measurement tool: bench2 UCI command (iters arg) with inline
  cntvct/mono ground truth; move-type debug line.

2026-08-17 board eval-machinery profile (CCOUNT ground truth):
- Board esp_timer_get_time() deltas are INFLATED ~1000x when called from
  the console task while searcher threads exist (~1.85ms blocking per call,
  cross-core esp_timer lock contention with the waiting searcher task).
  The SEARCH's own esp_timer timing (searcher task, console idle) is
  truthful: go depth 8 = 40,342 nodes / 5474ms claimed vs 6.0s wall incl.
  ~0.5s serial overhead -> 7,369 nps REAL (2-thread 7,100 anchor confirmed).
- Desktop had the same disease (gettimeofday deltas inflated, inline
  cntvct/mono truthful). Lesson: esp_timer_get_time deltas are unreliable
  in cross-task contexts; use CCOUNT (Xtensa) / cntvct (aarch64) inline.
- REAL board per-op costs (CCOUNT @240MHz):
  - pos make+unmake: 667 cycles (2.8us)
  - full make+eval+unmake: 21,214 cycles (88us)
  - eval feature updates: ~65us per op (2048 int16 updates @31ns/update)
  - nnue_evaluate (PIE accx_dot16): ~2.9us - already PIE, tiny
