  assembled by the espressif toolchain (unknown opcode) and are not in the
  S3 silicon's PIE (the full add/sub PIE is S2-only). Acc updates are
  memory-bound scalar (3.1 cycles/update warm, measured via CCOUNT) and
  cannot be vectorized on this chip. Board ~7.1-7.4k nps is near the
  practical ceiling; eval machinery is ~65% of the node budget, mostly
  irreducible flash-cache-bound row updates.
