[2026-08-21 17:10] ROOT CAUSE of "moves did nothing" found + fixed: onPointerDown compared fen piece color ("w"/"b") against myColor ("white"/"black") - never equal, so tapping a piece could never select it (tap AND drag both dead). Existed since v1; every prior browser test called handleMove() directly, bypassing the pointer pipeline. Also fixed en route: tap-to-move (second tap on a legal target now completes the move; plain taps keep the selection), setPointerCapture threw on synthetic pointers, pointercancel cleanup, /state clock write-back compounding bug (drained value stored without re-anchoring -> accelerating drain -> flag in minutes; now display-only with sticky flag at true zero). Verified through REAL dispatched PointerEvents: tap-tap e2e4 WORKS, drag d2d4 WORKS, engine replies, 0 JS errors; full 19-check two-browser suite green; seat released after tests.

[2026-08-21 19:40] Polish pass + THE root cause of the broken sessions found and fixed. (A) httpd death: the hand-rolled socket-based DNS responder broke the httpd listen socket after its first answered query (accept -> EBADF, web dead until reboot) - every session died ~1 min in. Replaced with a raw-lwip-UDP responder (no task/fd); verified 149 DNS queries + 149 HTTP requests concurrently all pass; multi-boot soak clean. (B) The gray blob over the board: CSS .dot rule for legal-move markers collided with the header status LED (#dot), stretching it into a giant translucent ellipse on EVERY device; scoped to .sq .dot. (C) Polish shipped: outlined-white/filled-black glyph rendering with stroke (fixes washed-out/opposite-looking pieces), FLIP move animation, check highlight (client-side attack detection), captured-piece bars + material lead, move/capture/check/end sounds + haptics, Resign endpoint + button, Flip board button, formatted history (e2-e4 / e4xd5 / e8=Q). Verified: tap-tap + drag through real pointer events, 19/19 two-browser suite, screenshots reviewed at each step. Seat cleared after testing.

[2026-08-24 05:30] PAIRED-FUSED NNUE REBUILD (eval pipeline). Profile said 60% of instructions sat in add_piece/remove_piece/nnue_evaluate, so the evaluator got rebuilt: weight blob permuted at load into 384 contiguous [own|other] row pairs (the flip-based net's true partner of own-row f is 384+f with square^56 - not 384+f), all of a move's accumulator deltas applied to BOTH perspectives in one sweep, unmake rebuilds the inverse batch from the existing undo journal, and explicit SIMD everywhere (NEON host / SSE2 x86 / new PIE kernels on ESP32-S3 using zero-widen->s32 VADDS/VSUBS->narrow, because the S3 has no wrapping int16 vector add). Desktop verdict: bit-exact (4000/4000 evals identical; node/score/PV equality at depths 7+9 on 6 FENs; unit gate 18/18) and speed PARITY - Ir dropped 12%, D1 misses 17%, but wall clock dead even (3.30s vs 3.30s median): the old eval was memory-latency-bound, OOO had been hiding it; instruction profiles mislead. Strength gate desktop-vs-baseline 2+0.02 200 games: 39-42-119, Elo -5.2 +/- 30.7, LOS 36.9% - a coin flip, as bit-exactness predicts. Board verdict: the win lives here. Old firmware console bench 20554 nodes/2.5s (~8200 nps avg); new firmware completes depth 8 with node counts IDENTICAL to the desktop binary through depth 8 (27677 nodes) and reaches 36650+ within budget, ~14600 nps avg = ~1.8x node throughput. Hardware caught one real bug: PIE dispatch assumed removals-first ordering but ENPASSANT journals sub,add,sub and CASTLING sub,add,sub,add -> any ep/castle line corrupted accumulators by +/-2x a weight row (startpos bench showed cp -3247 garbage); fixed with order-independent index-pair dispatch + a boot-time apply()-decomposition selftest next to the kernel selftest (engine falls back to scalar C path if either ever fails). Board-vs-native gate: 3 clean games, no stalls/forfeits/illegal moves. Binaries: baseline md5 b2e8d19d25f7119c7aaf8c2ccf38f045, new md5 82b0b6c0134453ed0dba3fd50fe124a9. Design notes: docs/paired-fused-nnue.md.
[2026-08-24 06:45] BOARD ELO VALUE OF THE PAIRED-FUSED SPEEDUP measured (asymmetric-tc selfplay, same binary md5 82b0b6c0134453ed0dba3fd50fe124a9 both sides, tc 3.6+0.036 vs 2+0.02 = exactly the 1.8x node-throughput ratio the board gained): 126-15-99 [73.1%] over 240 games -> +173.9 +/- 34.3, LOS 100.0%, draw ratio 41.3%. So the rebuild is worth ~+174 Elo on the ESP32 (desktop: bit-exact, 0.0 +/- noise, gate said -5.2 +/- 30.7). Board position estimate: pre-rebuild anchor was ~2200-2400 blitz class (-579 +/- ~162 vs SF17 at 2+0.02); with +174 -> roughly 2350-2550 class on-device. Note: early SPRT probe stopped at 10 games claiming +301 +/- 340 - discarded, fixed-length match used instead.
[2026-08-24 07:30] BUG HUNT on paired-fused code. Found + fixed one real bug: Eval::push_delta's flat-blob fallback (board boot without PSRAM) resolved the other-perspective row as old[384+k], but pair k's partner is old[384+k+((k%64)^56)-(k%64)] (square flips between perspectives) - would have produced garbage evals had PSRAM allocation ever failed. Fix verified with an exhaustive 768-case index probe (all piece/square/color events vs original indexing): paired layout 0/768 wrong, fixed fallback 0/768 wrong, in-place PSRAM permute proven element-identical to the desktop copy permute. Re-verified end to end after rebuild: startpos eval 80, 1000-FEN differential identical, kiwipete depth-9 node equality (137488 nodes, e2a6), board ladder matches desktop through depth 8, ~14.7k avg nps unchanged, PIE selftests silent-pass on flash.

[2026-08-24 18:30] CORRECTION HISTORY (self-correcting static eval) built + gated + REJECTED after ~1900 games. Full component: pawn/non-pawn-pair int16 tables keyed by XOR piece-square keys maintained incrementally inside Eval (same make/unmake wrappers as the NNUE deltas), bound-gated depth-weighted gravity updates at node completion, application at staticeval/qs stand-pat, reset points mirroring history[] (ucinewgame/bench/tui/tests). Unit gate 18/18 with component installed; bench deterministic per FEN. Gates vs HEAD (2+0.02, 200g unless noted): shift-all-evals w/ exact-PV updates -19.1+/-29.9; main-search-only -31.4+/-30.8 (isolated update policy as the bug); bounded-only updates +12.2+/-29.5 LOS 79% at 200g but REFUTED by 600g replication of same binary: -33.1+/-17.6 LOS 0.0% (lesson: screen positives need replication); complexity-only variant (table magnitude -> futility/LMR margins, no eval shifts) -3.5+/-29.7 despite +15% nodes at fixed depth; qs-stand-pat-only full weights +1.7+/-29.5; half weights +5.2+/-30.3 then 600g replication -0.6+/-16.6 = exact parity. Verdict: within-game learning budget (thousands of nodes/move, tables cleared per game) is too small for signal to separate from noise before game end, and razor/RFP/futility margins are tuned tighter than any useful deflection (results.log passim). Tree reverted to HEAD, bit-exact bench 7,582,143 nodes restored. Full write-up: docs/correction-history.md; final variant diff archived in session /tmp/opencode/corrhist-variants/. Do not re-try without a persistent-across-games training story or longer TC gates.
