[2026-08-25 00:40] OUTPUT-LAYER SRAM STAGING (eval interface speed, bit-exact). Rationale: profiling showed 6.97M nnue_evaluate calls per long bench (0.92/node), the output pass costs ~450 ns/node (~35% of nps sits behind it), and on the board every eval re-reads its 1 KB of output weights + bias through flash-XIP while the feature rows already enjoy their permuted PSRAM copy. Change: boot-time stage of Network.output_weights[2]+bias into a 1088-byte internal-SRAM block (heap_caps_aligned_alloc, MALLOC_CAP_INTERNAL) with graceful fallback to blob pointers if allocation loses to more urgent users - same bytes either way, so results are bit-exact by construction. Desktop verdict: bench node count IDENTICAL (7,582,143) across rebuilds; unit gate 18/18. Board verdict: startpos console bench 18,773/18,781/18,829/18,843 nps vs same-day control firmware (staging compiled out) 17,722/17,743 = +5.9-6.2% node throughput under identical conditions; depth 9 reached in budget where control reaches 8-9 boundary. Board-vs-native gate: 4 games clean, no stalls/forfeits/illegal moves (board lost on merit as expected). 2-thread UCI smoke: 2/2 searches completed. NOT a strength change on desktop by design (bit-exact); on-device value follows the throughput->Elo curve (~+6% = roughly +10-15 Elo-class, cf. paired-fused 1.8x -> +173.9). ENVIRONMENTAL FINDINGS en route: (1) board console test suite currently aborts on ALL firmware variants including unmodified HEAD - deterministic 32KB internal pthread-stack alloc failure at t=9.1s inside run_tests()' allocate_threads; pre-existing, orthogonal to this item, needs its own session; (2) this dev Pi was auto-joining the board's DOG-CHESS AP (httpd client load) - disconnected + autoconnect off via nmcli. Binaries: desktop md5 after final build 4f9dd861b534b74394d70a04782d76e6-lineage (rebuilt); board esp32chesstest ELF f2895fd2-lineage. Design notes appended to docs/paired-fused-nnue.md lineage - see docs/output-layer-staging.md.

[2026-08-25 02:20] BOARD TEST-SUITE ABORT root-caused + fixed; thermal bench drift quantified. Symptom: console `test` aborted at t=9.1s on every firmware variant INCLUDING unmodified HEAD - pthread stack alloc of 32768 internal bytes failed inside run_tests()' thread churn, uncaught std::system_error -> abort -> reboot loop. Root cause chain: the web phases (SoftAP/httpd) permanently consumed the internal-SRAM headroom that used to absorb a 96 KB peak demand (tests thread 32K + two recreated searcher stacks 2x32K), all from CONFIG_PTHREAD_TASK_STACK_SIZE_DEFAULT=32768. Fixes: default pthread stack 32768->16384 (app/sdkconfig + sdkconfig.defaults), searchers get an explicit 28 KB block via esp_pthread_set_cfg around their creation (16 KB default clips qsearch hard: warm bench nodes fell 47k->39k at 16 KB; 28 KB recovers full depth), allocate_threads() catches per-thread creation failures with partial-entry rollback and degrades to fewer searchers instead of aborting, run_tests() skips with a message instead of rebooting when no stack is available. Verified: suite now passes the old instant-abort point and runs to completion territory (the NNUE-perft tail legitimately takes >1 h on board); board-vs-native games clean; 2-thread UCI smoke clean. THERMAL FINDING (explains the "~14,700 nps" reference): absolute board bench nps swings ~15% with board temperature - cool-boot session measured staged/control = 18.8k/17.7k, hot evening session same pair = 15.5k/14.6k; the staging delta reproduces as +4.8-6.2% across both states, and the historical 14.7k was evidently a warm-board number. Only same-session pairs are meaningful for board benches. Also: dev Pi was auto-joining DOG-CHESS AP during benches (httpd client load) - disconnected, autoconnect off.
