[22:05:59] VERDICT ab-stagedpicker-p1-rep-20260825-212158: REJECT: H0 (no improvement) - llr -2.3 <= -2.2
[2026-08-25 21:35] PHASE 2 PROJECT 1 - STAGED MOVE PICKER: REJECTED after two full
  SPRTs. Implementation: TT move + previous-iteration capture claimed to the front
  (list's own encoding only), winning/equal captures+promotions SEE-gated lazily,
  quiets by history stack (piece-to+butterfly+continuation), losing captures last;
  selection sort replaced by staged incremental extraction; extensions/LMR/qsearch
  untouched. Two real bugs found and fixed during bring-up before any gate: (1) pins
  emitted directly can inject moves that are not pseudo-legal here (root feeds
  best_moves[] entries two iterations old) - old score-boost scheme could never do
  that; (2) Move::operator== ignores type bits, so playing a TT-stored twin of a
  generated quiet feeds make_move a lie (CAPTURE-typed onto an empty square) and
  corrupts the board - pins must claim the movelist's own object. Both fixes are
  knowledge for any future picker work; the diff is reverted but archived in this
  session log. Bench tax: none measured (same-session interleaved pairs parity).
  Unit gate 18/18. SPRT TC=2+0.02 Hash=8 a/b=0.1 elo1=20 CONC=1 vs Dog-phase2-base
  (fd8cef65): run 1 A=new B=base 196-171-392 [0.516] 800g cap, Elo +9.6 +/- 16.7,
  LOS 86.9%, llr -0.128 -> cap-revert by llr sign; pre-committed replication run:
  800g fresh sample, H0 accepted at -2.3, Elo -2.8 +/- 20.7, LOS 39.5%. Pooled ~+3 =
  noise. Lesson: the classic staged-picker gains (history-ordered quiets, losing
  captures demoted) were already harvested by the orderA rebuild - up-front scoring
  plus capture/butterfly/continuation tables leave this refactor nothing measurable
  to eat. Do not re-attempt without a new ordering signal or a much faster node.
