  Verdict for the whole project: this engine's time management at 2+0.02 is already
  at its measured optimum, same conclusion as the pruning margins. The adaptive
  interpolation (itd_moves/depth) plus the half-rule apparently captures everything
  easy-move would save; windows are so small (~50-70 ms) that neither trigger fires
  often enough to matter. Tree reverted to fd8cef65 bit-exact. Do not re-gate TM
  tweaks at bullet TCs; if anything, revisit only under longer TCs where windows
  give the triggers room.
