[2026-08-26 01:50] PHASE 2 PROJECT 4 - TT REDESIGN (widened key): REJECTED at the
  gate, with a conditional caveat. Layout: 8 -> 12 byte entries, 16 -> 32 bit
  signature (low 32 bits of the zobrist hash; low bits kept so the unit suite's
  hash-0 aliasing pins still hold), M:18/flags/age policy untouched - replacement,
  aging and generation semantics are exactly the accepted ttaging form, only the
  key width and entry shape moved. Index derivation unchanged. Unit gate: first cut
  failed the tt test because the high-32-bit signature broke the crafted hash
  0..3 aliasing expectations - switched to low-32 and got 18/18 without touching the
  test. Same-session bench pairs showed MORE nodes in fixed time (1.45M vs 1.3M
  band) and higher nps: fewer corrupted-entry searches is real. SPRT TC=2+0.02
  Hash=8 a/b=0.1 elo1=20 CONC=1 vs fd8cef65: H0 accepted after ~350 games, Elo
  -9.7 +/- 25.9, LOS 23.1%. Reading: Hash=8 buys 1.00M x 8-byte entries vs 699k
  x 12-byte ones - the ~30% capacity loss costs more at blitz node counts than
  collision integrity gains, because a collided entry mostly wastes a probe or gets
  rejected by is_legal_move rather than losing material outright. Conditional
  takeaway for a future attempt: the trade should flip where tables actually fill -
  long TCs or Hash>=32 on desktop, multi-million-node positions. Do not re-gate at
  bullet with small hashes. Tree reverted; deterministic long bench reproduces
  baseline exactly (7,441,088 nodes).
[2026-08-26 01:55] PHASE 2 SUMMARY: four projects, four reverts, zero accepted.
  P1 staged picker +9.6 then -2.8 (two full 800-game SPRTs), P2 time management
  package -8.6 and easy-move-only -5.0, P3 proper singular extensions -6.5 (with
  the R3R1K1 d19 sweep killing an unpreflighted variant again, 5-0 lifetime),
  P4 TT widening -9.7. The engine's search was already at a measured local optimum:
  every canonical modern-search item has now been probed against the orderA state
  and lost or tied. The ordering rebuild from Aug 25 appears to have consumed the
  remaining slack. All binaries reverted to fd8cef65-equivalent source (HEAD);
  long-bench node parity verified after each revert. Knowledge bank: pin-injection
  and Move type-bit traps for pickers, LOWERBOUND requirement for SE, capacity-vs-
  integrity economics for TT layout, TM non-slack at bullet.

[2026-08-26 15:30] MOVE-ORDERING REBUILD SPEED CAMPAIGN - STEP 0 FRESH PROFILE + STEP 1 BIT-EXACT RECOVERY ATTEMPT: REJECTED (no ship), honest locality verdict logged.
  STEP 0 - re-profile, same tree (fd8cef65-equivalent, ORDER_TABLE_READS verified true at search.cpp:30 before and after every bench round - the Aug 25 FALSE incident not repeated):
    Desktop callgrind (Pi 4, aarch64, short bench startpos depth 9, deterministic fixed-depth 68,082 nodes, cp 78, PV e2e4 e7e5 g1f3 b8c6 d2d4 e5d4 f3d4 d7d5 d4c6 b7c6 b1c3):
      baseline Ir 261,540,837 total; move_evaluater 6,848,602 (2.62% of total; 4,638,072 + 2,210,530 split across the LTO clones). The Aug 25 profile that predated the rebuild is stale, but the shape holds: eval+make/unmake dominate Ir (~45%), search() 3-4%, qs 1-2%, move_evaluater 2-3%. AGENTS.md warning stands - Ir misleads for this latency-bound eval; D1/DL misses are the real cost, and callgrind --cache-sim on this short bench shows move_evaluater D1mr 1.4% / DLmr 0.4% because the 17k-node working set fits in cache. The wall tax is PSRAM on board and DRAM latency on desktop, not Ir.
      Desktop wall nps (short bench, startpos 2.5s iterative deepening, same-session pairs, Pi load 7.4 ondemand governor, helium + two opencode sessions - noisy, so numbers are illustrative not gate-grade):
        baseline all-reads 573,116 nps mean (4-round interleaved: 548,480 / 571,574 / 571,805 / 600,606). Ablation builds via -DORDER_{CAP,BF,CONT}_READS=0 added alongside ORDER_TABLE_READS (defaults 1, shipping cannot drift reads-disabled): nocap 582,029 (+1.55%), nobf 575,330 (+0.39%), nocont 583,156 (+1.75%) mean. Single-round long bench (depth 10, 50 FENs, 7.44M nodes deterministic) was worse: node counts shift with ordering (7.44M all vs 7.78M nocap) so nps conflates speed with early-cutoff node savings; not used for split. Takeaway: per-table wall deltas on this loaded Pi sit inside the ~5-10% thermal/load swing; no table dominates. Callgrind says cont's previous_move() optional cost is near-zero Ir; bf/cap are similar.
    Board bench (bench 2.5s startpos, single-thread, via USB serial, same-session doctrine):
      Baseline warm pre-flash (shipping fd8cef65 firmware, 1-thread): 45,861 nodes / 18,290 nps, depth 9. Same board after three flashes and 20 min of desk time: baseline re-flashed 37,731 / 15,044 nps - the 15% thermal swing the Aug 25 log quantifies (cool 18.8k/17.7k vs hot 15.5k/14.6k) is real. Only same-session pairs within one warm window are truth. bench2 CCOUNT truth lines (esp_timer lies across tasks) confirm pos-only microbench, but ordering cost is not isolated there - the bench wall nps is the truth for the 3.3% read tax. The Aug 25 alternating-flash pair 18,916 -> 18,283 = -3.3% board, 573k -> 608k = -5.7% desktop remains the reference; re-measured same-session deltas this run sit in the same band when thermal is controlled.

  STEP 1 - bit-exact, same bytes, cheaper addressing:
    Attempted: (a) cache side/prevTo/hasPrev per node in sort_movelist_compare (constructor hoists side_to_move() and previous_move() once per node), (b) reuse MVV-LVA victim type for capture history so capture scoring does one piece_on instead of two, (c) drop always-true bounds checks (idx>=0 && idx<size) keeping only null-pointer guards.
    Variant (a) grew sort_movelist_compare by 12 bytes (Color+Square+bool, 28KB searcher stack *64 levels = +768 bytes). Desktop ladder passed (startpos d9 cp78 68,082 nodes, PV identical; two more FENs d8 also exact). Unit gate 18/18. But board flash of that variant: first bench 38,109 / 15,196 nps, second 38,067 / 15,098 - then second bench attempt hung the console (searcher stack tight at 28KB, the Aug 25 fix comment in main.cpp:281 warns every byte under ~28KB costs depth; the extra 768 bytes pushed qsearch capping and triggered the yield gate/WDT path). Reverted (a), kept (b)+(c) as safe subset "S1b" (victim reuse + bounds drop only, no extra stack).
    S1b: desktop d9 Ir 260,498,498 total (-0.40% vs 261,540,837 baseline), move_evaluater -223,478 (-3.26%). Fixed-depth ladders three FENs exact, 18/18 unit. Desktop short bench interleaved S1b vs baseline mean 470,511 vs 466,020 (+0.96% mean, but per-round swing -32% to +40% on loaded Pi - noise dominates). Board S1b flashed: 37,802 / 15,072 nps and 37,867 / 15,098 (two benches, warm). Baseline re-flashed same session: 37,731 / 15,044. Delta +0.2% = parity, below the 1.7% half-tax bar (half of 3.3%). The board's PSRAM stall cost dominates; shaving one extra piece_on (board array in internal SRAM, cheap) and two integer branches does not move the needle.

  Layout verdict (the trap in the brief): merging butterfly [side][from][to] (16KB) with continuation [prevTo][to] (8KB) into one table keyed [side][from][prevTo][to] is 2*64*64*64 *2B = 2,097,152 bytes. The board carves ordering tables from one 33KB PSRAM block per searcher (allocate_threads heap_caps_aligned_alloc 16, 33KB) next to the 6MB TT and weight copy; internal SRAM cannot fund 2MB, PSRAM budget does not have 2MB to spare per searcher. No static interleaving can co-locate bf[from][to] and cont[prevTo][to] for all (from,prevTo) pairs without the 4D expansion. Honest answer: locality cannot improve without changing what is read. The three tables live at 0, 9216, 25600 offset within the block (32B-aligned), bf and cont rows are 128 bytes each; a quiet move touches two distant PSRAM lines (bf row + cont row) plus one internal-SRAM history row. That is the tax.

  Decision: no bit-exact ship. The 3.3% board / 5.7% desktop read tax stands. Recovery via cheaper addressing is ~0.4% Ir, ~0% board wall, under the 1.7% bar. The next lane is the gated reduction (one variant per SPRT, 200 games TC=2+0.02 Threads=1 Hash=8): cont-only drop on ESP32 (smallest desktop signal + PSRAM-local, one PSRAM line saved per quiet move) or int8 packing with redesigned gravity. Not bundled. Fresh profile recorded here is itself the deliverable: further speed work should target the eval/make/unmake path (callgrind top: nnue_evaluate 14.5%, make/unmake 20%+), not move ordering, unless a reduction wins its SPRT.

  Tree reverted to baseline (fd8cef65-equivalent, HEAD). No code shipped. ORDER_TABLE_READS true verified in shipping position. Submodule fathom 2251e9974d5e1c77f09e35015fc325098e586e2c pinned.
